Z||000000||RiceBurner515||12-07-2000||07:02 PM||||okay, i know there is hours of reading about engine swaps and so forth, but sorry, i have no time for that. All i need to know is what engines will bolt right up to my 85 SE 4cyl. 5-spd tranny WITHOUT ANY major mods to anything in the engine or compartment, the easiest and will fit the engine mounts? i want a V6 or V8. what is the cheapest and what car will i find the engines in? But i don't want a 2.8, i want 3.0-3.4, i also heard of 4L's swap (4.9, 4.8, 4.7, etc.) Thanks SO MUCH!!! <BR>so~&gt; cheap, easy, no mods to car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||12-07-2000||07:24 PM||||Hey I'm in the same boat, I have the Automatic Transmition though, same car and year.... I was thinking a older 3.8, i guess it bolts right up but from what i have been told way to much work to get it to run right, Quad 4 I was thinking would be good but kit is too expensive, right now      I am thinking about a Caddy engine... but somehting just doesnt seem right that how easy it would go in...... ehh let me know<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-07-2000||07:25 PM||||It may be difficult to swap out an iron duke with a low cost v6 engine easily.  If you find a cheap 3.4 bolt on, there will be other modifdications required for the swap.  Then you may have a tired 3.4 in your Fiero for $1000.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000003||theogre||12-07-2000||10:45 PM||||Only a V6, the stock one and a couple others based on about the same block,will drop in as far as the structural stuff goes. All others will require some kind of work on the cradle at least.<P>All the conversions including the stock V6 will require major rework of the electrical system.||||reg||1
